{"id": "EUVD-2026-59375", "enisaUuid": "fcd48d64-ec51-3739-8355-19825e622bc0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndmaengine: Fix possible use after free\n\nIn dma_release_channel(), check chan->device->privatecnt after call\ndma_chan_put(). However, dma_chan_put() call dma_device_put() which could\nrelease the last reference of the device if the DMA provider is already\ngone and hence free it.\n\nFixes it by moving dma_chan_put() after the check.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:57:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:25", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/444f96066937f3fdf0e79b53289cff223c7d638b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab438a9efb9042c79d2f8db28a326d55feb8591f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9bdc8dce4068dadbdf7cf5ad6d4983e2afffedce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5876f38b67a309c00628942cb25679749b53b397", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3b0240483dc977dbec4f3bc7a5383d4691ecb625", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/329ec20a86091d2a6e5b4fe507545e7d678a22a2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0bc191050c3253da8ef4bfaf157c44efed6e22cd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/92f853f0645aebf1d05d333e97ab7c342ace1892"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72476", "GHSA-3wch-675q-fgx7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "047c2b8c-621f-3753-a4dd-0f9e57fe0bda", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0f571515c332e00b3515dbe0859ceaa30ab66e00 <92f853f0645aebf1d05d333e97ab7c342ace1892"}, {"id": "1476887b-2b97-3ed0-a6b7-29b55a8a0ab4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0f571515c332e00b3515dbe0859ceaa30ab66e00 <ab438a9efb9042c79d2f8db28a326d55feb8591f"}, {"id": "17115538-dc4d-3387-ae57-9f899f8b262f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.30"}, {"id": "17383